Revision history for RNG.

[Unreleased]
    - Return false string seeds as always-true RNG::Seed objects without
      changing their string value or the seed expansion used for replay.
      Raw state seeds use an RNG::Seed::Raw subclass of RNG::SeedBase.
    - Preserve the historical true zero-seed return for Drand48 and recognize
      "0 but true" as zero when it is reused with that provider.
    - Check seed replay across all providers and add published PCG vectors.
      Correct the XSL-RR variants to output from the updated state.
    - Add PCG RXS-M-XS 64/64 and PCG XSL-RR 128/64 MCG and LCG variants.
      The LCG increment is now derived from the seed, selecting a stream.
      Select a variant when constructing RNG::PCG. Use native 128-bit
      arithmetic where the compiler target supports it, with a two-word
      fallback for other targets.
    - Add the RNG factory and reusable die, dice, chooser, and weighted
      distribution objects, using Vose's alias method for weighted choices.
    - Make rand_bytes the portable provider protocol and require providers to
      be objects implementing rand_bytes and srand.
    - Update the XS provider versions for the new protocol and high-bit
      drand48 byte adapter.
    - Add the XS RNG::Drand48 provider for comparison with Perl's built-in
      drand48-based generator and the ${^RNG} interface.
    - Add the XS RNG::HMAC_DRBG provider, with deterministic and secure
      operating-system-seeded modes and an optional prediction-resistance
      policy.
    - Add the XS RNG::Wyrand and RNG::Xoshiro providers, including the
      optional native U01 callbacks used by the core fast path.
    - Normalize ordinary seeds as UTF-8 octets and add RNG::Seed and
      RNG::SeedBase for exact replayable raw state material.  Secure HMAC_DRBG
      initialization returns a redacted seed token.
    - Add state-seed construction from standard HMAC_DRBG entropy, nonce, and
      personalization inputs for deterministic test vectors.

0.01  2026-08-16
    - Initial version.
